ntrol of an opponent of your choice.\\n{2}, {T}: Draw a card, then you may put a land card from your hand onto the battlefield. Pendant of Prosperity's owner draws a card, then that player may put a land card from their hand onto the battlefield.", 'Prevent all combat damage that would be dealt to attacking artifact creatures you control.\\nWhenever one or more artifact creatures enter the battlefield under your control, draw a card. This ability triggers only once each turn.', 'Prevent all combat damage that would be dealt to you this turn. For each 1 damage prevented this way, create a 2/1 white and black Inkling creature token with flying.', 'Reach\\nCreature spells you cast cost {X} less to cast, where X is the amount of life you gained this turn.\\n{T}: You gain 2 life.', 'Return all artifact cards from your graveyard to the battlefield. They gain haste until end of turn.', "Return six target nonland permanents to their owners' hands.", "Return target creature or land card from a graveyard to its owner's hand. You gain 6 life.", "Return target instant or sorcery card from your graveyard to your hand. Volcanic Vision deals damage equal to that card's mana value to each creature your opponents control. Exile Volcanic Vision.", 'Search your library for a basic land card, put that card onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', 'Search your library for up to three basic land cards, put them onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle. You gain 7 life.', 'Search your library for up to two basic land cards, reveal those cards, put one onto the battlefield tapped and the other into your hand, then shuffle.', 'Secluded Steppe enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {W}.\\nCycling {W} ({W}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)', 'Shuffle your library. Then exile the top card of your library. Until end of turn, you may play that card without paying its mana cost.\\nStorm (When you cast this spell, copy it for each spell cast before it this turn.)', "Simic Growth Chamber enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Simic Growth Chamber enters the battlefield, return a land you control to its owner's hand.\\n{T}: Add {G}{U}.", "Split second (As long as this spell is on the stack, players can't cast spells or activate abilities that aren't mana abilities.)\\nDestroy target artifact or enchantment.", 'Tap target creature.\\nMetalcraft — If you control three or more artifacts, exile that creature.', 'Target player draws X cards and loses X life.', "Target player draws X cards plus an additional card for each time they've cast a commander from the command zone this game.", 'Temple of Epiphany enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Temple of Epiphany enters the battlefield, scry 1.\\n{T}: Add {U} or {R}.', 'Temple of Malady enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Temple of Malady enters the battlefield, scry 1.\\n{T}: Add {B} or {G}.', 'Temple of Mystery enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Temple of Mystery enters the battlefield, scry 1.\\n{T}: Add {G} or {U}.', 'Temple of Silence enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Temple of Silence enters the battlefield, scry 1.\\n{T}: Add {W} or {B}.', 'Temple of Triumph enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Temple of Triumph enters the battlefield, scry 1.\\n{T}: Add {R} or {W}.', 'The owner of target nonland permanent shuffles it into their library, then draws two cards.', 'This spell costs {1} less to cast for each creature on the battlefield.\\nBlasphemous Act deals 13 damage to each creature.', 'This spell costs {8} less to cast if you have eight or more instant and/or sorcery cards in your graveyard.\\nWard {8}\\nMagecraft — Whenever you cast or copy an instant or sorcery spell, target creature has base power and toughness 8/8 until end of turn.', 'This spell costs {X} less to cast, where X is the amount of life you gained this turn.\\nTrample\\nAt the beginning of your end step, if you gained life this turn, you may cast Sproutback Trudge from your graveyard.', 'Trample\\nAt the beginning of your end step, create a number of Food tokens equal to the number of nontoken creatures you had enter the battlefield under your control this turn.\\n{1}, Sacrifice a Food: Target creature gains indestructible until end of turn. Tap it.', 'Trample\\nInferno Project enters the battlefield with X +1/+1 counters on it, where X is the total mana value of instant and sorcery cards in your graveyard.', 'Trample\\nLandfall — Whenever a land enters the battlefield under your control, you may create a 4/4 green Beast creature token.', 'Trample\\nWhen Gluttonous Troll enters the battlefield, create a number of Food tokens equal to the number of opponents you have. (Food tokens are artifacts with "{2}, {T}, Sacrifice this artifact: You gain 3 life.")\\n{1}{G}, Sacrifice another nonland permanent: Gluttonous Troll gets +2/+2 until end of turn.', 'Trample\\nWhenever a player casts a spell, put a +1/+1 counter on Managorger Hydra.', "Trample\\nWhenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, Erratic Cyclops gets +X/+0 until end of turn, where X is that spell's mana value.", "Trample\\n{3}{R}, Sacrifice an artifact: Bosh, Iron Golem deals damage equal to the sacrificed artifact's mana value to any target.", 'Tranquil Thicket enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {G}.\\nCycling {G} ({G}, Discard this card: Draw a card.)', "Untap Victory Chimes during each other player's untap step.\\n{T}: A player of your choice adds {C}.", 'Vigilance, protection from creatures\\nWhenever a creature deals combat damage to you, destroy that creature. Create a 1/1 white and black Spirit creature token with flying.', 'Vigilance\\nWhenever Sun Titan enters the battlefield or attacks, you may return target permanent card with mana value 3 or less from your graveyard to the battlefield.', 'Vigilance\\n{1}, Sacrifice an artifact: Target creature you control gets +2/+0 until end of turn.\\n{X}, {T}, Exile an artifact card with mana value X from your graveyard: Create two tokens that are copies of the exiled card. Activate only as a sorcery.', 'Ward {2} (Whenever this creature becomes the target of a spell or ability an opponent controls, counter it unless that player pays {2}.)\\nIf one or more tokens would be created under your control, twice that many of those tokens are created instead.', "When Archaeomancer's Map enters the battlefield, search your library for up to two basic Plains cards, reveal them, put them into your hand, then shuffle.\\nWhenever a land enters the battlefield under an opponent's control, if that player controls more lands than you, you may put a land card from your hand onto the battlefield.", "When Author of Shadows enters the battlefield, exile all opponents' graveyards. Choose a nonland card exiled this way. You may cast that card for as long as it remains exiled, and you may spend mana as though it were mana of any color to cast that spell.", "When Champion of Wits enters the battlefield, you may draw cards equal to its power. If you do, discard two cards.\\nEternalize {5}{U}{U} ({5}{U}{U}, Exile this card from your graveyard: Create a token that's a copy of it, except it's a 4/4 black Zombie Naga Wizard with no mana cost. Eternalize only as a sorcery.)", "When Coiling Oracle enters the battlefield, reveal the top card of your library. If it's a land card, put it onto the battlefield. Otherwise, put that card into your hand.", "When Coveted Jewel enters the battlefield, draw three cards.\\n{T}: Add three mana of any one color.\\nWhenever one or more creatures an opponent controls attack you and aren't blocked, that player draws three cards and gains control of Coveted Jewel. Untap it.", 'When Elite Scaleguard enters the battlefield, bolster 2. (Choose a creature with the least toughness among creatures you control and put two +1/+1 counters on it.)\\nWhenever a creature you control with a +1/+1 counter on it attacks, tap target creature defending player controls.', 'When Fractal Harness enters the battlefield, create a 0/0 green and blue Fractal creature token. Put X +1/+1 counters on it and attach Fractal Harness to it.\\nWhenever equipped creature attacks, double the number of +1/+1 counters on it.\\nEquip {2}', 'When Ichor Wellspring enters the battlefield or is put into a graveyard from the battlefield, draw a card.', 'When Meteor Golem enters the battlefield, destroy target nonland permanent an opponent controls.', 'When Mycosynth Wellspring enters the battlefield or is put into a graveyard from the battlefield, you may search your library for a basic land card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.', "When Myr Battlesphere enters the battlefield, create four 1/1 colorless Myr artifact creature tokens.\\nWhenever Myr Battlesphere attacks, you may tap X untapped Myr you control. If you do, Myr Battlesphere gets +X/+0 until end of turn and deals X damage to the player or planeswalker it's attacking.", 'When Oreskos Explorer enters the battlefield, search your library for up to X Plains cards, where X is the number of players who control more lands than you. Reveal those cards, put them into your hand, then shuffle.', "When Pia Nalaar enters the battlefield, create a 1/1 colorless Thopter artifact creature token with flying.\\n{1}{R}: Target artifact creature gets +1/+0 until end of turn.\\n{1}, Sacrifice an artifact: Target creature can't block this turn.", 'When Radiant Fountain enters the battlefield, you gain 2 life.\\n{T}: Add {C}.', 'When Reef Worm dies, create a 3/3 blue Fish creature token with "When this creature dies, create a 6/6 blue Whale creature token with \'When this creature dies, create a 9/9 blue Kraken creature token.\'"', 'When Scholarship Sponsor enters the battlefield, each player who controls fewer lands than the player who controls the most lands searches their library for a number of basic land cards less than or equal to the difference, puts those cards onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffles.', 'When Solemn Simulacrum enters the battlefield, you may search your library for a basic land card, put that card onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.\\nWhen Solemn Simulacrum dies, you may draw a card.', "When Stalking Leonin enters the battlefield, secretly choose an opponent.\\nReveal the player you chose: Exile target creature that's attacking you if it's controlled by the chosen player. Activate only once.", 'When Terastodon enters the battlefield, you may destroy up to three target noncreature permanents. For each permanent put into a graveyard this way, its controller creates a 3/3 green Elephant creature token.', 'When Thopter Engineer enters the battlefield, create a 1/1 colorless Thopter artifact creature token with flying.\\nArtifact creatures you control have haste. (They can attack and {T} as soon as they come under your control.)', "When Together Forever enters the battlefield, support 2. (Put a +1/+1 counter on each of up to two target creatures.)\\n{1}: Choose target creature with a counter on it. When that creature dies this turn, return that card to its owner's hand.", 'When Wildfire Devils enters the battlefield and at the beginning of your upkeep, choose a player at random. That player exiles an instant or sorcery card from their graveyard. Copy that card. You may cast the copy without paying its mana cost.', 'When you cast this spell, create a 10/10 colorless Eldrazi creature token.', 'Whenever Blossoming Bogbeast attacks, you gain 2 life. Then creatures you control gain trample and get +X/+X until end of turn, where X is the amount of life you gained this turn.', "Whenever Etali, Primal Storm attacks, exile the top card of each player's library, then you may cast any number of spells from among those cards without paying their mana costs.", "Whenever Ruxa, Patient Professor enters the battlefield or attacks, return target creature card with no abilities from your graveyard to your hand.\\nCreatures you control with no abilities get +1/+1.\\nFor each creature you control with no abilities, you may have that creature assign its combat damage as though it weren't blocked.", 'Whenever Scrap Trawler or another artifact you control is put into a graveyard from the battlefield, return to your hand target artifact card in your graveyard with lesser mana value.', "Whenever Verdant Sun's Avatar or another creature enters the battlefield under your control, you gain life equal to that creature's toughness.", 'Whenever a Kraken, Leviathan, Octopus, or Serpent you control deals combat damage to a player, create a 9/9 blue Kraken creature token.', 'Whenever a creature you control dies, you gain 1 life and draw a card.', "Whenever a nontoken creature enters the battlefield under an opponent's control this turn, create a token that's a copy of that creature.", 'Whenever a player casts a spell, you may put a +1/+1 counter on Forgotten Ancient.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, you may move any number of +1/+1 counters from Forgotten Ancient onto other creatures.', "Whenever a player casts an instant or sorcery spell, put a number of charge counters on Geometric Nexus equal to that spell's mana value.\\n{6}, {T}, Remove all charge counters from Geometric Nexus: Create a 0/0 green and blue Fractal creature token. Put X +1/+1 counters on it, where X is the number of charge counters removed this way.", 'Whenever an artifact enters the battlefield under your control, you may discard a card. If you do, draw a card.', "Whenever an opponent attacks you and/or one or more planeswalkers you control, exile the top card of that player's library. You may play that card for as long as it remains exiled, and you may spend mana as though it were mana of any color to cast it.", 'Whenever an opponent casts their second spell each turn, you create a Treasure token.', "Whenever another nontoken creature you control dies, you may return it to the battlefield face down under its owner's control. It's a Forest land. (It has no other types or abilities.)", 'Whenever one or more creatures attack, you may have target attacking creature gain double strike until end of turn.', "Whenever you cast a spell from your hand, reveal the top X cards of your library, where X is that spell's mana value. You may cast a spell with mana value X or less from among cards revealed this way without paying its mana cost. Put the rest on the bottom of your library in a random order.", "Whenever you cast a spell with {X} in its mana cost, put two charge counters on Elementalist's Palette.\\n{T}: Add one mana of any color.\\n{T}: Add {C} for each charge counter on Elementalist's Palette. Spend this mana only on costs that contain {X}.", 'Whenever you cast an artifact spell, you may pay {2}. If you do, create a 0/0 colorless Construct artifact creature token with "This creature gets +1/+1 for each artifact you control."', 'Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, create a 2/2 blue Drake creature token with flying.', "Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, create an X/X colorless Construct artifact creature token, where X is that spell's mana value.\\n{3}{U}{U}, Exile Metallurgic Summonings: Return all instant and sorcery cards from your graveyard to your hand. Activate only if you control six or more artifacts.", 'Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, you may copy that spell. You may choose new targets for the copy.', 'Whenever you gain life, each opponent loses 1 life.', 'Whenever you gain life, put that many +1/+1 counters on Ageless Entity.', 'Whenever you gain life, target opponent loses that much life.', 'Whenever you gain life, you may pay {2}. If you do, create a 4/4 green Fungus Beast creature token with trample.', 'Whenever you gain life, you may pay {X}, where X is less than or equal to the amount of life you gained. If you do, draw X cards.', "Whenever you're dealt damage, put that many charge counters on Sun Droplet.\\nAt the beginning of each upkeep, you may remove a charge counter from Sun Droplet. If you do, you gain 1 life.", 'You draw X cards and you lose X life, where X is the mana value of a commander you own on the battlefield or in the command zone.', 'You draw three cards and you lose 3 life.', 'You gain 2 life. Each creature gets -X/-X until end of turn, where X is the amount of life you gained this turn.', 'You have no maximum hand size.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, you gain 1 life for each card in your hand.', 'You have no maximum hand size.\\n{T}: Add {C}.', 'You may activate abilities of creatures you control as though those creatures had haste.\\n{1}, {T}: Untap target creature.', "You may cast Rout as though it had flash if you pay {2} more to cast it. (You may cast it any time you could cast an instant.)\\nDestroy all creatures. They can't be regenerated.", 'You may have Sculpting Steel enter the battlefield as a copy of any artifact on the battlefield.', '[+1]: Add {R}{R}{R}. Spend this mana only to cast instant or sorcery spells.\\n[+1]: Discard up to three cards, then draw that many cards.\\n[−8]: You get an emblem with "You may cast instant and sorcery spells from your graveyard. If a spell cast this way would be put into your graveyard, exile it instead."', '[+1]: Create a 3/3 green Beast creature token.\\n[−3]: Draw cards equal to the greatest power among creatures you control.\\n[−6]: Create a 6/6 green Wurm creature token for each land you control.', "[+1]: Put a loyalty counter on Gideon, Champion of Justice for each creature target opponent controls.\\n[0]: Until end of turn, Gideon, Champion of Justice becomes a Human Soldier creature with power and toughness each equal to the number of loyalty counters on him and gains indestructible. He's still a planeswalker. Prevent all damage that would be dealt to him this turn.\\n[−15]: Exile all other permanents.", '[+1]: You draw a card and you lose 1 life.\\n[−3]: Destroy target creature.\\n[−8]: Target opponent gets an emblem with "Whenever a player draws a card, you lose 2 life."', '[+2]: Discard up to two cards, then draw that many cards.\\n[−2]: Sacrifice an artifact. If you do, return target artifact card from your graveyard to the battlefield.\\n[−10]: You get an emblem with "Whenever an artifact is put into your graveyard from the battlefield, return that card to the battlefield at the beginning of the next end step."\\nDaretti, Scrap Savant can be your commander.', '{1}, {T}: Add {G}{U}.', '{1}, {T}: Add {U}{R}.', '{1}, {T}: Add {W}{B}.', '{1}, {T}: Choose another target creature. Put a number of +1/+1 counters on it equal to the amount of life you gained this turn or the amount of life you lost this turn, whichever is greater. Activate only as a sorcery.', "{2}, {T}: Reveal the top card of your library. If it's a creature card, create a 1/1 green Saproling creature token. If it's a land card, put that card onto the battlefield under your control. If it's a noncreature, nonland card, you gain 2 life.", "{2}, {T}: You gain 5 life. Shuffle Elixir of Immortality and your graveyard into their owner's library.", "{2}{R}, {T}: Create a token that's a copy of target creature card in your graveyard, except it's an artifact in addition to its other types. It gains haste. Sacrifice it at the beginning of the next end step.", "{2}{W}, {T}, Sacrifice Dispeller's Capsule: Destroy target artifact or enchantment.", '{3}, Sacrifice Burnished Hart: Search your library for up to two basic land cards, put them onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', '{B}, Pay 2 life: Draw a card.', "{G}{U}: Target creature can't be blocked this turn. If that creature is a Snake, it gets +2/+2 until end of turn.", "{T}, Discard a card: Up to one target creature can't be blocked this turn.\\nWhenever Key to the City becomes untapped, you may pay {2}. If you do, draw a card.", '{T}, Sacrifice a creature: Put two +1/+1 counters on target creature.\\n{T}, Remove a counter from a creature you control: Create a Treasure token.\\n{T}, Sacrifice an artifact: Create a 2/1 white and black Inkling creature token with flying.\\n{3}{B}: Untap Fain, the Broker.', '{T}, Sacrifice an artifact: Reveal cards from the top of your library until you reveal an artifact card. Put that card onto the battlefield and the rest on the bottom of your library in a random order. Audacious Reshapers deals damage to you equal to the number of cards revealed this way.', "{T}: Add one mana of any color in your commander's color identity.", "{T}: Add one mana of any color in your commander's color identity.\\nSacrifice Commander's Sphere: Draw a card.", '{T}: Add one mana of any color that a land an opponent controls could produce.', '{T}: Add one mana of any type that a land you control could produce. If Incubation Druid has a +1/+1 counter on it, add three mana of that type instead.\\n{3}{G}{G}: Adapt 3. (If this creature has no +1/+1 counters on it, put three +1/+1 counters on it.)', '{T}: Add {C}. You gain 1 life.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}, {T}, Sacrifice Mind Stone: Draw a card.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}, {T}, Sacrifice an artifact: You gain 1 life.', "{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}, {T}: Add one mana of any color in your commander's color identity. If you spend this mana to cast your commander, it enters the battlefield with a number of additional +1/+1 counters on it equal to the number of times it's been cast from the command zone this game.", "{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}, {T}: Add one mana of any color. When you spend this mana to cast your commander, scry X, where X is the number of times it's been cast from the command zone this game.", '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}, {T}: Put a storage counter on Mage-Ring Network.\\n{T}, Remove any number of storage counters from Mage-Ring Network: Add {C} for each storage counter removed this way.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{2}, {T}, Sacrifice a Desert: Exile all graveyards.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{2}, {T}: Each player draws a card.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{2}, {T}: Target commander gains lifelink until end of turn.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{2}{R}{W}, {T}: Target creature gains double strike until end of turn.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{3}{G}, {T}, Sacrifice Blighted Woodland: Search your library for up to two basic land cards, put them onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', "{T}: Add {C}.\\n{4}, {T}: Target creature can't be blocked this turn.", '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{5}{U}, {T}, Sacrifice Blighted Cataract: Draw two cards.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{7}, {T}, Sacrifice Unstable Obelisk: Destroy target permanent.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{G}{U}, {T}: Put a +1/+1 counter on each creature that entered the battlefield this turn.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{R}{W}, {T}: Target creature gets +2/+0 and gains vigilance and haste until end of turn.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}, Sacrifice a creature: You gain 1 life.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {B} or {G}. Activate only if you control a Swamp.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {B} or {G}. Llanowar Wastes deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {B} or {G}. Talisman of Resilience deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {G} or {U}. Yavimaya Coast deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {R} or {W}. Battlefield Forge deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {U} or {R}. Shivan Reef deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {U} or {R}. Talisman of Creativity deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {W} or {B}. Activate only if you control a Swamp.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {W} or {B}. Caves of Koilos deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {C}{C}.', '{T}: Add {C}{C}. Activate only if you control five or more lands.', '{T}: Add {C}{C}.\\n{2}, {T}, Sacrifice Hedron Archive: Draw two cards.', '{T}: Add {R} or {W}.\\n{R/W}{R/W}{R/W}{R/W}, {T}, Sacrifice Boros Locket: Draw two cards.', '{T}: Add {R}.', '{T}: Add {R}. When that mana is spent to cast a red instant or sorcery spell, copy that spell and you may choose new targets for the copy.', '{T}: Add {R}.\\nAs Cursed Mirror enters the battlefield, you may have it become a copy of any creature on the battlefield until end of turn, except it has haste.', '{T}: Add {W}.', '{T}: Choose a player. That player adds one mana of any color they choose.', '{T}: Draw a card. Activate only if you created a token this turn.\\n{8}, {T}, Sacrifice Idol of Oblivion: Create a 10/10 colorless Eldrazi creature token.', '{T}: Draw two cards. Target opponent gains control of Humble Defector. Activate only during your turn.', '{T}: Put a +1/+1 counter on each artifact creature you control.', "{U}, {T}: Until your next turn, target creature an opponent controls can't be blocked. Goad that creature. (Until your next turn, that creature attacks each combat if able and attacks a player other than you if able.)", "{W}, Sacrifice Soul Snare: Exile target creature that's attacking you or a planeswalker you control.", '{X}, {T}: Exile target creature card with mana value X from a graveyard. Create a 0/0 green and blue Fractal creature token. Put X +1/+1 counters on it. Activate only as a sorcery.', '{X}{G}, {T}: Arashi, the Sky Asunder deals X damage to target creature with flying.\\nChannel — {X}{G}{G}, Discard Arashi: Arashi deals X damage to each creature with flying.', "{X}{X}{G}: Monstrosity X. (If this creature isn't monstrous, put X +1/+1 counters on it and it becomes monstrous.)\\nWhen Hydra Broodmaster becomes monstrous, create X X/X green Hydra creature tokens."]
flavor: ['"A crafter must imbue her weapon with part of her soul—something the Phyrexians are incapable of doing."\\n—Melira', '"A fine example of addition by subtraction."\\n—Deekah, professor of fractal theory', '"A regression to ancient forms? A glimpse of future evolutions? Or a fleeting alteration of the present?"\\n—Vorel of the Hull Clade', '"A richer people could give more but they could never give as much."', '"All peoples treasure a place where the weary traveler may drink in peace."\\n—Ajani Goldmane', '"Approach my tower on bended knee or depart from it as ash upon the wind."\\n—Gadwick, the Wizened', '"Arise, great one, and cleanse the world of our enemies!"', '"As I desire, so it shall be."\\n—Nicol Bolas', '"As long as my hand holds a blade, there\'s hope for a pure Mirrodin once again."', '"Belong in a museum? I think we should let relics belong wherever they please!"\\n—Quintorius, Lorehold mage-student', '"Blood is constant. Every drop I drink, someone must bleed."\\n—Vradeen, vampire nocturnus', '"Body and spirit are sworn enemies. They will take any excuse to be rid of each other."\\n—Tariel, Reckoner of Souls', '"Bottled life. Not as tasty as I\'m used to, rather stale, but it has the same effect."\\n—Baron Sengir', '"Center of the Sea, Eye of the World, Shrine of Enlightenment. Seek it for answers. Seek it for healing. Seek it and return transformed."\\n—Scroll fragment from the ruins of Minamo', '"Conquering your first world is the hardest, after all. My power grew as I moved from world to world, taking anything that would make the next taking easier."\\n—Ob Nixilis', '"Despite their bravado, mortals are fragile. If Zendikar is to endure, its lords must save it."\\n—Drana, Kalastria bloodchief', '"Dig over there, you bolthead!"', '"Don\'t think of it as debt. Think of it as an investment in yourself."\\n—Diriga, demon bursar', '"Don\'t worry, there\'s plenty for everyone."\\n—Vickon, Eleventh Company battlemage', '"Draw out your fear, but don\'t let it control you. You\'re in charge now."', '"End this. What I seek is far greater."\\n—Elesh Norn, Grand Cenobite', '"Even in death, we never stop growing."', '"Flee all you like. The further you run the more firmly I feel your heartbeat."', '"Fleshy, with just a hint of leather. A fine vintage."', '"From this day forward, we confront this world together, lifting each other up."', '"Give up these unnatural weapons, these scrolls. Heart and mind and fist are enough."\\n—Zyd, Kamahlite druid', '"Good ideas don\'t take time. They take a lot of bad ideas first."\\n—Ral Zarek', '"Her voice is justice, clear and relentless."\\n—Akroma, angelic avenger', '"Holy places are no longer sanctuary from death, and death is no longer sanctuary from anything."\\n—Thalia, Knight-Cathar', '"Hone the knife and mourn the least. Three chimes to sound the sweet, grim feast."\\n—Barrow witch incantation', '"I came seeking a challenge. All I found was you."\\n—Zurgo, khan of the Mardu', '"I find its symmetry pleasing. It rids our world of offensive refuse while disposing of itself."\\n—Dolomarus, Proctor of the Clean', '"I hope to meet Jaya Ballard someday. I think we\'d get along."\\n—Chandra Nalaar', '"I know a good idea when I see one."', '"I never imagined I\'d lay eyes on a creature that makes Gyruda look small and harmless!"\\n—Lukka', '"I prefer loyalty to be a matter of respect, not of magic. But one does what one must."\\n—Kaalia of the Vast', '"It has been my experience that disasters like to strike in pairs."', '"It was a strange morning. When we awoke, we found our trees transformed. We didn\'t know whether to water them or polish them."\\n—Pulan, Bant orchardist', '"It\'s us against the world. Forever."', '"Ixalli\'s fertile rays enliven us all. Each of us is a testament to the sun\'s strength and love."\\n—Chitlati, Lightning Rider', '"Jarad fancies himself king of the undercity, but he\'s merely king of rot."', '"Little flower twirl and bloom, arise from this your rocky tomb. Little warrior slash and brawl, be born again to free us all."', '"Me? I\'m just an innocent bystander!"', '"Monsters dwell in every heart. We only think civilization tames them." ―Euphemia, Nexus watcher', '"Nature is a wonderful engineer but works far too slowly for my tastes."', '"On vile wings and bloody wind, the swarm will rise."\\n—Skyclave inscription', '"Our glorious infection has taken hold."\\n—Elesh Norn, Grand Cenobite', '"Our revered ancestor Seshiro gave us wisdom greater than poison and fangs."', '"Reality, when broken down, is just math."\\n—Deekah, professor of fractal theory', '"She will come back to me."', '"Silumgar\'s mind is a dark labyrinth, full of grim secrets and subtle traps."\\n—Siara, the Dragon\'s Mouth', '"So even the heart of our world has succumbed."\\n—Koth of the Hammer', '"Stand back. This part gets messy."', '"Sure, trudges smell like soggy death, but the mushrooms on their backs are the tastiest delicacy in Sedgemoor!"\\n—Gyome, Witherbloom chef', '"The League accepts no responsibility for former members and the damage they may cause."\\n—Maree, Izzet chamberlain', '"The continual rise of the downtrodden is as inevitable as vines usurping a forest."\\n—Vraska', '"The curse is broken."', '"The end is justified in being mean. Or something like that."', '"The heroes of the past nourish our spirits by their example—and nourish our crops by their decay."\\n—Jeddeg, philosopher of graves', '"The land grows only where the kami will it."\\n—Dosan the Falling Leaf', '"The seas are vast, but the skies are even more so. Why be content with one kingdom when I can rule them both?"', '"The unnatural pressures of life in this city are best withstood by lifeforms that adapt with unnatural swiftness."\\n—Momir Vig', '"The world is already run by all manner of machines. One day, they\'ll remind us of that fact."\\n—Sargis Haz, artificer', '"There is nothing so invigorating and stubbornly belligerent as the pure energy of life."\\n—Valentin, Witherbloom dean', '"Those who do not submit will be consumed."', '"Tools and artisans can be destroyed, but the act of creation is inviolate."\\n—Elspeth Tirel', '"We pass these along to our fellow soldiers to recognize deeds of valor. It won\'t stay with you for long."\\n—Alovnek, Boros guildmage', '"We train for the improbable, like lightning striking the same place twice, or striking everywhere at once."\\n—Nundari, Sea Gate militia captain', '"We trust in the scalelords, bringers of justice that none can escape."\\n—Urdnan, Dromoka warrior', '"We\'ve merged your life essence with that of several creatures at once. You\'re welcome."\\n—Speaker Trifon', '"What is mana but possibility, an idea not yet given form?"\\n—Jhoira, master artificer', '"When the land is angry, so are they."\\n—Nissa Revane', '"Why squabble for trinkets when we could be living large off all this gold?"\\n—Admiral Beckett Brass', '"With just a little added flair, your work could be truly spectacular. Let me show you."\\n—Nassari, Prismari dean', '"With precise coordination and enough blood spilled, one can be driven off, even brought down. But two . . . that\'s a lot of blood."\\n—Munda, ambush leader', '"You made it asymmetrical just to annoy me, didn\'t you?"\\n—Imbraham, Quandrix dean', '"You were once Mardu, so your body and will are strong. Now we must train your mind."\\n—Houn, Jeskai elder', '"You\'ve begun to understand the hedrons\' true purpose," said Ugin. "The Eldrazi can be imprisoned."\\n"And how did that work out last time?" asked Jace.', '"Your proofs were a bit nontraditional, but effective nonetheless. Full marks."', '"Your unsolicited words enrich us all. Please, continue."\\n—Yold, professor of cryptorelicology', "A Planeswalker's chronicle spans worlds and civilizations, each page a lifetime.", 'A blazing sun that never sets.', 'A circus acrobat in life, she kills with such fluid grace that even her victims are awed by her performance.', 'A last wisp of paradise in a fallen world.', 'A thousand years of history undone by one juvenile prank.', 'After years of research, he finally unlocked the formula for a perfect punch.', 'All seeds share a common bond, calling to each other across infinity.', 'An artificer once dropped one in a vault full of coins. She has yet to find it.', 'Another imminent battle subsided in busy snuffling and carefree rooting.', 'Art born from such raw emotion often takes on a life of its own.', 'As Glissa searches for the truth about Memnarch, Bosh searches to unearth the secrets of his past.', 'As subtle as a bogbeast\\n—Witherbloom expression meaning\\n"crude and clumsy"', 'As their supplies of etherium dwindled, mechanists sent gargoyles farther and farther afield in search of salvage.', 'As they fought the Eldrazi, many vampires learned to live among humans. Others were unable to make the adjustment.', 'Being trapped between two forms of unlife is a fate worse than mere death.', 'Blood magic is more artery than science.', 'Countless delights drift on the surface while dark schemes run below.', 'Devils sow grief and harvest glee.', 'First, whispers of ancient days. Then, visions of things to come.', 'For the Simic Combine, its sigil serves not as an emblem of honor but as a trademark. Its familiar image on any biological commodity attests to superb craftsmanship, ingenious innovation, and higher cost.', 'Forged by divine hands to wander mortal realms.', 'Golgari reclaimers resent the gorgons, begrudging the loss of so many fine nutrients locked away in stone.', 'He collects the precious metals, and then converts the rest to propellant.', 'Held aloft by metabolized magic, trygons are ravenous for sources of mystic fuel.', 'Her connection to the plane restored, Nissa felt the power of Zendikar surge through her.', 'Her plans may yet bear fruit.', "If it can't be had here, it can't be had on any world.", 'In their final moments, the demons gazed upon grace in its purest form.', 'Infinitely powerless.', "It contains the totality of Alhammarret's notes, theories, and ponderings.", "It feeds on the dark energies that course through the deep world—and on any other creature lured by the leyline's pull.", 'It harmonizes with the essence of its master.', 'It hears and answers every orison across Shadowmoor.', 'It started as a mere drop of water. The Magic Mirror crystallized it into much more.', 'It would be unfortunate if the key fell into the wrong hands.', 'Its blood is life. Its body is growth.', 'Its collapse is like the lashing out of a long-dead civilization that resents being forgotten.', 'Its courtyards are lit during every hour of the day so that night may never fall within its walls.', 'Its flight sets the sky itself on fire.', 'Jund feasts on the unprepared.', 'Knowledge demands sacrifice.', 'Kuldotha, wellspring of molten metal, temple of the goblin horde.', "Lost to time is the artificer's art of trapping light from a distant star in a ring of purest gold.", 'Nature grows solutions to its problems.', "No amount of solitary studying can replace a master's tutelage.", 'Once guarded by the Knights of the Reliquary, the tower stands now protected only by its own remoteness, its dusty treasures open to plunder by anyone.', 'Once, water ran here. Now only dust and ash fall from the clifftops.', 'One moment, conscious only of a sense of repose. The next moment, hearing the trudge of his own footsteps. He sighed and squinted into the glare ahead.', "Paradoxically, to tilt the massive jug for a sip, you'd need the energy of the giant's tonic.", 'Pests feed on carrion, mud, and one another.', 'Possession is eleven-tenths of the pirate code.', 'Quicksmiths are eager to jump from one project to the next, relying on flashes of inspiration rather than careful research.', 'Rumors quickly spread among thieves about a labyrinth without walls and a prize beyond all measures of worth.', "Serum was once derived from Mirrodin's blinkmoths, offering visions of inspiration. Now it is pulled from Phyrexian inkmoths, yielding visions of perfection.", 'Silverquill first-years welcome discomfort in the classroom, knowing it will prepare them for the years ahead.', "Silverquill's elite know how to offer a scathing rebuttal without uttering a word.", 'Snaking remnants of nature directed by a body of thought and progress, the oracles embody all that is Simic.', 'Some Strixhaven study groups are more welcoming than others.', "Some say the knowledge lost during the Ritual of Rebuking is returned through the well's waters.", 'Some timelines forever fray, branch, and intermingle. Others end abruptly.', 'Sounds of life beckon many a restless soul.', 'Spitting is the customary greeting between a creature and its magical impostor.', 'Structures built from darksteel yield to neither assault nor age.', "Students from other colleges are invited to visit Witherbloom's medical facilities. Not many do.", 'Sunhome—the stalwart shield, the towering sentinel, the seat of justice.', 'Taj-Nar, throne of Raksha Golden Cub, destined leader of the leonin prides.', "Tel-Jilad's sworn protectors are the trolls, yet more fearsome protectors were created by the Tangle itself.", 'The Izzet signet is redesigned often, each time becoming closer to a vanity portrait of Niv-Mizzet.', "The Locust God's children were numberless, relentlessly eating away every trace of the city's protection.", 'The Orzhov care not for repentance, only repayment.', 'The Quicksilver Sea hissed and bubbled at the indignity. The Vulshok shaman just smiled.', 'The best techniques outlive their creators.', 'The favored noisemaker of goblins ever since the wardens cracked down on explosives.', 'The first searchlights were given as gifts, symbols of cooperation, to the emissaries present at the signing of the Guildpact.', 'The impact sent the soldiers scattering—then something came out of the crater.', 'The kor send their thopter kites to see if the land is in a welcoming mood.', "The lammasu ruled the velds before the city grew. Now they roam Ravnica's skies, but their ancient enemies have not forgotten them.", 'The militia formed up in the central plaza awaiting the onslaught, but the giants never quite made it.', 'The mizzium-sphere array drove her mind deep into the thought field, where only the rarest motes of genius may be plucked.', 'The oil created the mycosynth. The mycosynth created New Phyrexia.', 'The sigil holds different meanings depending on its form and presentation. While some wear it as a sign of status, others wear it as a sign of debt.', 'The sky takes flight and the earth trembles.', "The spear thrown by Kytheon's own hand was the weapon that felled his friends.", 'The storm rages and the earth breaks.', 'The weapon wields the hand that holds it.', 'Those who bring nothing to the temple take nothing away.', "Though the spirits' bodies were ethereal, Agnur soon learned that their blades were quite solid—and razor-sharp.", 'Tomorrow belongs to those who prepare for it today.', "Ulamog's tentacles, their touch like burning ice, rummaged through his soul and stung his memories one by one.", 'Venser wondered if it could still be called a teleportation spell if the destination is oblivion.', "Vulshok mana rituals echo the day when the red sun burst through Mirrodin's surface to take its place in the heavens.", 'What goes into the vivipods never quite matches what comes out.', "What is a sliver of one's soul compared to unimaginable wealth?", 'When the last scrap of flesh is scoured away, the Curse of Wandering ends. Then the dead may sleep.', 'When the winds blow out of the abyss, death is the only harvest.']
